/-!
# Freeness of the stalks of a coherent module whose completion has finite free stalks

Let `S` be an algebraization situation with Noetherian base ring `A`, ideals `I ≤ 𝔞`, open
subscheme `U = Spec A ∖ V(𝔞)` and ideal sheaf `ℐ = I 𝒪_U`, and assume `I = (f)` is principal
with `f` a nonzerodivisor of `A`. Let `(F_m)` be a coherent adic system along `ℐ` whose stalks
are finite free over the infinitesimal neighbourhoods, that is, every `F_{m,x}` is a finite free
`𝒪_{U,x} / ℐ_x ᵐ⁺¹`-module. If a coherent module `𝒢` on an open `V ⊆ U` has
`𝒢 / (ℐ|_V) ᵐ⁺¹ 𝒢 ≅ F_m|_V` for all `m`, compatibly with the transition maps, then `𝒢` is free
at every point `y` of `V` at which the germ of `f` fails to be a unit.

The proof is the stalkwise one. Write `R = 𝒪_{V,y}`, a Noetherian local ring, `M = 𝒢_y`, a
finite `R`-module since `𝒢` is coherent, and `T` for the germ of `f` in `R`; `T` is a
nonzerodivisor because `f` is one in `A` and the local rings of `U` are localizations of `A`,
and `T` lies in the maximal ideal by hypothesis. The isomorphism of adic systems gives, at level
`n`, a chain of identifications
`M / Tⁿ⁺¹M ≃ (𝒢 / (ℐ|_V) ⁿ⁺¹ 𝒢)_y ≃ (F_n|_V)_y ≃ F_{n,x} ≃ (𝒪_{U,x} / ℐ_x ⁿ⁺¹)ʳ`,
whose last two steps live over the local ring of `U` at the image point `x` of `y` rather than
over `R`. The two rings are identified by `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.stalkIso`, the
comparison of stalks across a restriction is semilinear over that identification, and the two
semilinearities cancel, so the composite is an `R`-linear equivalence
`M / Tⁿ⁺¹M ≃ (R / (Tⁿ⁺¹))ʳ`. Freeness of `M` is then
`Module.free_of_free_quotient_pow_smul`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.FreeStalkQuotient.nonempty_linearEquiv_pi_of_addEquiv_of_ringEquiv` — a finite free
  presentation of a module transports, along a semilinear additive bijection over a ring
  isomorphism, to a finite free presentation of the quotient of the source by the corresponding
  ideal.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.stalkRingEquiv` — the local ring of an open subscheme at a
  point, identified with the local ring of the ambient scheme at the image point, together with
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.stalkMap_stalkRingEquiv` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.stalkRingEquiv_stalkMap` saying that it inverts the stalk map
  of the inclusion.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.germOfBaseOpen` — the germ at a point of an open `V ⊆ U` of the
  function on `U` attached to an element of the base ring.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.stalk_comap_idealOnOpen_eq_span_germOfBaseOpen` — for `I = (f)` the
  stalk of `ℐ|_V` at a point of `V` is generated by the germ of `f` there.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.nonempty_linearEquiv_quotient_germOfBaseOpen_pow_smul` — the chained
  linear equivalence `𝒢_y / Tⁿ⁺¹𝒢_y ≃ (R / (Tⁿ⁺¹))ʳ` above.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.free_stalk_of_hasFiniteFreeStalks_completion` — the stalk of `𝒢` at `y`
  is a free `𝒪_{V,y}`-module.

## Implementation notes

The hypothesis on the system `(F_m)` is recorded, as in
`Stacks.Algebraization.hasFiniteFreeStalks_completionFunctor_of_isFiniteLocallyFree`, as the
existence of a linear equivalence `F_{m,x} ≃ (𝒪_{U,x} / ℐ_x ᵐ⁺¹)ʳ` for some `r`; that is the
stalkwise content of finite local freeness over the `m`-th infinitesimal neighbourhood, and it
is all the argument uses.

The ring identification is handled once, in
`Stacks.FreeStalkQuotient.nonempty_linearEquiv_pi_of_addEquiv_of_ringEquiv`, by composing the
semilinear additive bijection with the ring isomorphism of quotients it induces and checking
linearity of the composite by hand; this avoids carrying semilinear maps and their
`RingHomInvPair` instances through the geometric part of the chain.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DXW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DXW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EIK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EIK)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.ModuleSkyscraper (modulesStalkFunctor)

universe u

namespace Stacks.FreeStalkQuotient

/-- **Transporting a finite free presentation along a ring isomorphism.** Let `eR : R ≃+* R'` be
a ring isomorphism carrying an ideal `I` of `R` onto an ideal `I'` of `R'`, let `A` be an
`R`-module and `B` an `R'`-module, and let `φ : A ≃+ B` be an additive bijection which is
semilinear over `eR`. A presentation of `B` as a finite power of `R' / I'` then presents `A` as
a finite power of `R / I`: compose `φ` with the presentation and with the ring isomorphism
`R / I ≃+* R' / I'` induced by `eR`, whose semilinearity cancels that of `φ`. -/
theorem nonempty_linearEquiv_pi_of_addEquiv_of_ringEquiv
    {R R' : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing R'] (eR : R ≃+* R')
    {I : Ideal R} {I' : Ideal R'} (hI : I' = I.map (eR : R →+* R'))
    {A : Type u} [AddCommGroup A] [Module R A] {B : Type u} [AddCommGroup B] [Module R' B]
    (φ : A ≃+ B) (hφ : ∀ (a : R) (z : A), φ (a • z) = eR a • φ z)
    {r : ℕ} (ψ : B ≃ₗ[R'] (Fin r → R' ⧸ I')) :
    Nonempty (A ≃ₗ[R] (Fin r → R ⧸ I)) := by
  classical
  have key : ∀ (a : R) (d : Fin r → R' ⧸ I') (i : Fin r),
      (Ideal.quotientEquiv I I' eR hI).symm (eR a • d i) =
        a • (Ideal.quotientEquiv I I' eR hI).symm (d i) := by
    intro a d i
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (d i)
    rw [← hw]
    have hl : eR a • Ideal.Quotient.mk I' w = Ideal.Quotient.mk I' (eR a * w) := rfl
    rw [hl, Ideal.quotientEquiv_symm_mk, Ideal.quotientEquiv_symm_mk, map_mul,
      RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
    rfl
  refine ⟨AddEquiv.toLinearEquiv
    ((φ.trans ψ.toAddEquiv).trans
      (AddEquiv.piCongrRight fun _ : Fin r => (Ideal.quotientEquiv I I' eR hI).symm.toAddEquiv))
    fun a z => ?_⟩
  have h1 : (φ.trans ψ.toAddEquiv) (a • z) = eR a • (φ.trans ψ.toAddEquiv) z := by
    show ψ (φ (a • z)) = eR a • ψ (φ z)
    rw [hφ a z, map_smul]
  show (AddEquiv.piCongrRight fun _ : Fin r => (Ideal.quotientEquiv I I' eR hI).symm.toAddEquiv)
      ((φ.trans ψ.toAddEquiv) (a • z)) =
    a • (AddEquiv.piCongrRight fun _ : Fin r =>
      (Ideal.quotientEquiv I I' eR hI).symm.toAddEquiv) ((φ.trans ψ.toAddEquiv) z)
  rw [h1]
  funext i
  exact key a _ i

end Stacks.FreeStalkQuotient

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens

/-! ### The local ring of an open subscheme -/

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (V : X.Opens) (y : V.toScheme)

/-- **The local ring of an open subscheme at a point is the local ring of the ambient scheme at
the image point**, as a ring isomorphism. This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.stalkIso` read as an isomorphism of rings, with the image point
spelled as the image of `y` under the base map of the inclusion `V ⟶ X`. -/
def stalkRingEquiv : V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y ≃+* X.presheaf.stalk (V.ι.base y) :=
  (V.stalkIso y).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv

/-- **The stalk map of the inclusion of an open subscheme inverts the identification of local
rings**: the identification is the `hom` of the comparison isomorphism and the stalk map is its
`inv`. -/
theorem stalkMap_stalkRingEquiv (r : V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y) :
    (V.ι.stalkMap y).hom (stalkRingEquiv V y r) = r := by
  rw [show V.ι.stalkMap y = (V.stalkIso y).inv from (stalkIso_inv V y).symm]
  exact (V.stalkIso y).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.symm_apply_apply r

/-- **The identification of local rings inverts the stalk map of the inclusion of an open
subscheme.** -/
theorem stalkRingEquiv_stalkMap (w : X.presheaf.stalk (V.ι.base y)) :
    stalkRingEquiv V y ((V.ι.stalkMap y).hom w) = w := by
  rw [show V.ι.stalkMap y = (V.stalkIso y).inv from (stalkIso_inv V y).symm]
  exact (V.stalkIso y).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.apply_symm_apply w

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

/-! ### The germ of a base element on an open of the complement -/

variable (S : AlgebraizationSituation.{u})

/-- The germ at a point `y` of an open `V ⊆ U` of the global function on `U` determined by an
element `a` of the base ring: the image of `Stacks.Algebraization.germOfBase` under the stalk map
of the inclusion `V ⟶ U`. -/
def germOfBaseOpen (V : S.U.toScheme.Opens) (y : V.toScheme) (a : S.A) :
    V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y :=
  (V.ι.stalkMap y).hom (germOfBase S (V.ι.base y) a)

/-- **The germ of a base element on an open of `U` is the image of its germ on `U`** under the
identification of the local ring of `U` at the image point with the local ring of `V` at the
point. -/
theorem stalkRingEquiv_germOfBaseOpen (V : S.U.toScheme.Opens) (y : V.toScheme) (a : S.A) :
    Scheme.Opens.stalkRingEquiv V y (germOfBaseOpen S V y a) =
      germOfBase S (V.ι.base y) a :=
  Scheme.Opens.stalkRingEquiv_stalkMap V y _

/-- **The germ of a nonzerodivisor of the base ring is a nonzerodivisor.** The germ on `V` is
the image of the germ on `U`, which is a nonzerodivisor by
`Stacks.Algebraization.germOfBase_mem_nonZeroDivisors`, under a ring isomorphism. -/
theorem germOfBaseOpen_mem_nonZeroDivisors {f : S.A} (hf : f ∈ nonZeroDivisors S.A)
    (V : S.U.toScheme.Opens) (y : V.toScheme) :
    germOfBaseOpen S V y f ∈ nonZeroDivisors (V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y) := by
  refine mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_injective
    (f := Scheme.Opens.stalkRingEquiv V y)
    (Scheme.Opens.stalkRingEquiv V y).injective ?_
  rw [stalkRingEquiv_germOfBaseOpen S V y f]
  exact germOfBase_mem_nonZeroDivisors S hf (V.ι.base y)

/-- **A base element whose germ on `U` is not a unit has a germ on `V` which is not a unit.** -/
theorem germOfBaseOpen_mem_maximalIdeal {f : S.A} (V : S.U.toScheme.Opens) (y : V.toScheme)
    (hy : germOfBase S (V.ι.base y) f ∈
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.U.toScheme.presheaf.stalk (V.ι.base y))) :
    germOfBaseOpen S V y f ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y) := by
  have h := (IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal _).1 hy
  refine (IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal _).2 fun hu => h ?_
  rw [← stalkRingEquiv_germOfBaseOpen S V y f]
  exact hu.map (Scheme.Opens.stalkRingEquiv V y)

/-- **When `I = (f)` the stalk of `ℐ|_V` at a point of `V` is generated by the germ of `f`
there.** The stalk of a restricted ideal sheaf is the image of the stalk of the ideal sheaf under
the stalk map (`AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_comap`), the stalk of `ℐ` is generated by
the germ of `f` on `U` (`Stacks.Algebraization.stalk_idealOnOpen_eq_span_germOfBase`), and the
image of a principal ideal is generated by the image of its generator. -/
theorem stalk_comap_idealOnOpen_eq_span_germOfBaseOpen {f : S.A} (hI : S.I = Ideal.span {f})
    (V : S.U.toScheme.Opens) (y : V.toScheme) :
    IdealSheafData.stalk ((idealOnOpen S).comap V.ι) y =
      Ideal.span {germOfBaseOpen S V y f} := by
  rw [IdealSheafData.stalk_comap, stalk_idealOnOpen_eq_span_germOfBase S hI, Ideal.map_span,
    Set.image_singleton]
  rfl

/-! ### The chained linear equivalence at a stalk -/

/-- **The quotient `𝒢_y / Tⁿ⁺¹ 𝒢_y` is a finite power of `𝒪_{V,y} / (Tⁿ⁺¹)`.**

Let `S` be an algebraization situation with `I = (f)` principal, let `(F_m)` be a coherent adic
system along `ℐ = I 𝒪_U` whose stalks are finite free over the infinitesimal neighbourhoods, let
`𝒢` be a coherent module on an open `V ⊆ U` and let `e` identify the completion of `𝒢` along
`ℐ|_V` with the restriction of `(F_m)` to `V`. Writing `T` for the germ of `f` at `y`, the
`n`-th level of `e` gives an `𝒪_{V,y}`-linear equivalence
`𝒢_y / Tⁿ⁺¹𝒢_y ≃ (𝒪_{V,y} / (Tⁿ⁺¹))ʳ` for some `r`.

The quotient on the left is the stalk of the `n`-th term of the completion, by
`Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerQuotientStalkLinearEquiv` and
`Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor_obj`; `e` identifies that with the stalk at `y` of
`F_n|_V`, which is the stalk of `F_n` at the image point `x` of `y`, semilinearly over
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.stalkIso`; and the hypothesis on the system presents the latter
as a finite power of `𝒪_{U,x} / ℐ_x ⁿ⁺¹`. The ring identification carries `(Tⁿ⁺¹)` to
`ℐ_x ⁿ⁺¹`, so the two semilinearities cancel. -/
theorem nonempty_linearEquiv_quotient_germOfBaseOpen_pow_smul {f : S.A}
    (hI : S.I = Ideal.span {f})
    (F : Stacks.Coherent.CoherentAdicSystems (idealOnOpen S))
    (hfree : ∀ (m : ℕ) (x : S.U.toScheme), ∃ r : ℕ,
      Nonempty ((modulesStalkFunctor S.U.toScheme x).obj (F.obj.obj (op m))
        ≃ₗ[S.U.toScheme.presheaf.stalk x]
        (Fin r → (S.U.toScheme.presheaf.stalk x ⧸
          IdealSheafData.stalk (idealOnOpen S) x ^ (m + 1)))))
    (V : S.U.toScheme.Opens)
    (G : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.CoherentModules V.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (e : ((completionFunctor V.toScheme ((idealOnOpen S).comap V.ι)).obj G).obj ≅
          F.obj ⋙ AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor V.ι)
    (y : V.toScheme) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ r : ℕ, Nonempty (((modulesStalkFunctor V.toScheme y).obj G.obj ⧸
        (Ideal.span {germOfBaseOpen S V y f ^ (n + 1)} •
          (⊤ : Submodule (V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y)
            ((modulesStalkFunctor V.toScheme y).obj G.obj))))
      ≃ₗ[V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y]
        (Fin r → (V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y ⧸
          Ideal.span {germOfBaseOpen S V y f ^ (n + 1)}))) := by
  classical
  have : G.obj.IsQuasicoherent := isQuasicoherent_of_isCoherent G.obj
  obtain ⟨r, ⟨ψ⟩⟩ := hfree n (V.ι.base y)
  refine ⟨r, ?_⟩
  -- The stalk of the restricted ideal sheaf, to the `(n+1)`-st power.
  have hJ : IdealSheafData.stalk ((idealOnOpen S).comap V.ι) y ^ (n + 1) =
      Ideal.span {germOfBaseOpen S V y f ^ (n + 1)} := by
    rw [stalk_comap_idealOnOpen_eq_span_germOfBaseOpen S hI V y, Ideal.span_singleton_pow]
  -- The `n`-th level of `e`, with the completion's `n`-th term spelled as an ideal-power
  -- quotient.
  have hobj : ((completionFunctor V.toScheme ((idealOnOpen S).comap V.ι)).obj G).obj.obj (op n) =
      idealPowerQuotient ((idealOnOpen S).comap V.ι) (n + 1) G.obj :=
    completionFunctor_obj V.toScheme ((idealOnOpen S).comap V.ι) G n
  let iso : idealPowerQuotient ((idealOnOpen S).comap V.ι) (n + 1) G.obj ≅
      (F.obj.obj (op n)).restrict V.ι := eqToIso hobj.symm ≪≫ e.app (op n)
  -- The `𝒪_{V,y}`-linear half of the chain.
  let Φ : ((modulesStalkFunctor V.toScheme y).obj G.obj ⧸
      (Ideal.span {germOfBaseOpen S V y f ^ (n + 1)} •
        (⊤ : Submodule (V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y)
          ((modulesStalkFunctor V.toScheme y).obj G.obj))))
      ≃ₗ[V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y]
      (modulesStalkFunctor V.toScheme y).obj ((F.obj.obj (op n)).restrict V.ι) :=
    (Submodule.quotEquivOfEq _ _ (congrArg (fun K : Ideal (V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y) =>
        K • (⊤ : Submodule (V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y)
          ((modulesStalkFunctor V.toScheme y).obj G.obj))) hJ.symm)).trans
      ((idealPowerQuotientStalkLinearEquiv ((idealOnOpen S).comap V.ι) (n + 1) G.obj y).trans
        ((modulesStalkFunctor V.toScheme y).mapIso iso).toLinearEquiv)
  -- The comparison of the stalk on `V` with the stalk on `U`.
  let Ψ := Scheme.Modules.restrictStalkAddEquiv V.ι (F.obj.obj (op n)) y
  refine Stacks.FreeStalkQuotient.nonempty_linearEquiv_pi_of_addEquiv_of_ringEquiv
    (Scheme.Opens.stalkRingEquiv V y) ?_ (Φ.toAddEquiv.trans Ψ) ?_ ψ
  · have hg : (Scheme.Opens.stalkRingEquiv V y : V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y →+*
        S.U.toScheme.presheaf.stalk (V.ι.base y)) (germOfBaseOpen S V y f) =
        germOfBase S (V.ι.base y) f := stalkRingEquiv_germOfBaseOpen S V y f
    rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, map_pow, hg, ← Ideal.span_singleton_pow,
      ← stalk_idealOnOpen_eq_span_germOfBase S hI]
  · intro a z
    have h := Scheme.Modules.restrictStalkAddEquiv_smul V.ι (F.obj.obj (op n)) y
      (Scheme.Opens.stalkRingEquiv V y a) (Φ z)
    rw [Scheme.Opens.stalkMap_stalkRingEquiv V y a] at h
    have hΦ : Φ (a • z) = a • Φ z := map_smul Φ a z
    show Ψ (Φ (a • z)) = _
    rw [hΦ]
    exact h

/-! ### Freeness of the stalk -/

/-- **A coherent module whose completion is a system with finite free stalks is free at every
point where the germ of `f` is not a unit.**

Let `S` be an algebraization situation with `I = (f)` principal and `f` a nonzerodivisor of the
base ring, and let `(F_m)` be a coherent adic system along `ℐ = I 𝒪_U` all of whose stalks are
finite free over the infinitesimal neighbourhoods -- the stalkwise content of finite local
freeness of `F_m` over `𝒪_U / ℐ ᵐ⁺¹`. If a coherent module `𝒢` on an open `V ⊆ U` has its
completion along `ℐ|_V` isomorphic, as an adic system, to the restriction of `(F_m)` to `V`,
then `𝒢_y` is a free `𝒪_{V,y}`-module at every `y ∈ V` whose germ of `f` lies in the maximal
ideal.

The local ring `𝒪_{V,y}` is Noetherian local, `𝒢_y` is a finite module over it because `𝒢` is
coherent, the germ `T` of `f` is a nonzerodivisor lying in the maximal ideal, and
`Stacks.Algebraization.nonempty_linearEquiv_quotient_germOfBaseOpen_pow_smul` presents every
`𝒢_y / Tⁿ⁺¹𝒢_y` as a finite power of `𝒪_{V,y} / (Tⁿ⁺¹)`; so
`Module.free_of_free_quotient_pow_smul` applies. -/
theorem free_stalk_of_hasFiniteFreeStalks_completion {f : S.A} (hI : S.I = Ideal.span {f})
    (hnzd : f ∈ nonZeroDivisors S.A)
    (F : Stacks.Coherent.CoherentAdicSystems (idealOnOpen S))
    (hfree : ∀ (m : ℕ) (x : S.U.toScheme), ∃ r : ℕ,
      Nonempty ((modulesStalkFunctor S.U.toScheme x).obj (F.obj.obj (op m))
        ≃ₗ[S.U.toScheme.presheaf.stalk x]
        (Fin r → (S.U.toScheme.presheaf.stalk x ⧸
          IdealSheafData.stalk (idealOnOpen S) x ^ (m + 1)))))
    (V : S.U.toScheme.Opens)
    (G : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.CoherentModules V.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (e : ((completionFunctor V.toScheme ((idealOnOpen S).comap V.ι)).obj G).obj ≅
          F.obj ⋙ AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor V.ι)
    (y : V.toScheme)
    (hy : germOfBase S (V.ι.base y) f ∈
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.U.toScheme.presheaf.stalk (V.ι.base y))) :
    Module.Free (V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y)
      ((modulesStalkFunctor V.toScheme y).obj G.obj) := by
  have : G.obj.IsFiniteType := _root_.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent.isFiniteType
  have : Module.Finite (V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y)
      ((modulesStalkFunctor V.toScheme y).obj G.obj) :=
    _root_.SheafOfModules.finite_stalk V.toScheme.sheaf G.obj y
  exact Module.free_of_free_quotient_pow_smul
    (germOfBaseOpen_mem_maximalIdeal S V y hy)
    (germOfBaseOpen_mem_nonZeroDivisors S hnzd V y) _
    fun n => nonempty_linearEquiv_quotient_germOfBaseOpen_pow_smul S hI F hfree V G e y n

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
